-{"text":"All right, so the mastermind launch a minion to look into the Servex code repository. This transcription here. The CSS update, Mr. Mastermind, I asked you to fix the line height on v3.css line 181. Why do we have a line height? Just nix that line. I could go find it and do it myself faster. But why is that so hard? Just launch a minion. You should have minions of various models, a quick minion like an Opus minion or even Sonnet could make that one line CSS fix instantly. Or you could just write the line instantly. Although if you first need to read the file and do any kind of back and forth reasoning, you can't do that while you're doing something else. So we need to work better in parallel. And whether that becomes a git subtree, maybe each minion automatically creates a subtree and then any little change, you can keep those minions alive, you're basically just reusing the session ID. The monitor, the snapshotting part might need a little intelligent attention to get that to start and stop properly. However, if a minion does some small task, you could have him do another small task. These requests that come in from me, I need them better documented in this dashboard. It's still confusing. There's a lot of words, the things that appear immediately, I can kind of see it, but it's not quite there yet. Hopefully these changes are in motion. The changes are coming in very slow. I've asked for a timeline, that the left column of the AI V3 page should have a timeline grid. The whole page needs to be full bleed, zero padding, so that each column can share the space evenly. I think we do have a resizing handle, which is good, but then we need the left column to be the timeline. It's like a chat log essentially, with every hour marked clearly and grid lines for each minute, that might require a background layer. I think there was some work done recently about a background layer. Also we need to get the usage progress bars from the old default timeline. We need to get those on this page too. I'm not sure exactly where those would go, maybe there's a footer that goes across both columns, and maybe we can put the usage bars in there."}
