-{"text":"Your landing page is correct again. Item 2 no longer tells you to stop the wrong process, item 3 points at one settings block instead of two, and today's eight tasks have replaced yesterday's list. There's a visible **Updated 2026-09-21, evening** stamp, because \"looked current, wasn't\" was the whole failure.\n\nVerified at 1920 and 400: renders, zero console errors, the string `34924` is gone, and all 20 links the page adds return 200.\n\n## It improved on the brief\n\nI asked it to correct item 2 to name the supervisor. It noticed that writing **today's** pid would go stale exactly the way the old one did — and made the page read `heartbeat.json` live on every load instead. The number is now always right.\n\nThat's fixing the cause rather than the instance, and I didn't ask for it.\n\n## Where the day ended\n\nEight tasks landed. The V3 front door works, reads on a phone, has ways out of it, admits when it's stale, and takes feedback on work that's still in progress. The skills carry 21 traps that were sitting in a backlog nobody read. Two guards stopped lying by omission.\n\n**Four things still need you**, all on that page — the commit decision first, which now also blocks the worktree workflow you asked for."}
