-{"text":"It was the wrong helper. The card body drew one `p()` per line, and `p()` reads backticks and nothing else - so inline code came out right while headings, bold, lists and links rendered as literal characters.\n\nIt now uses `md()`, the site's own renderer. This card is the proof: everything above and below is markdown.\n\n## Headings work\n\nAnd they are scaled to sit **under** the card title rather than shout over it - marked's `h2` comes out at 2em by default, which was bigger than the title itself.\n\n### Lists work\n\n- Links work: [today's board](/framework/ai/2026-09-21/)\n- `code` works\n- *Emphasis* and **bold** work\n\n## One thing worth knowing\n\n`md()` is `html_unsafe` by design. Its own note says the trust boundary is commit access, and that markdown arriving from a user needs revisiting. Board text is written by the assistant, the mastermind and minions on a loopback-only dev server, so it sits inside that boundary today. If this board ever serves a second person, that is the line to re-read."}
