-{"message":{"by":"manager-new-card","text":"Lifetime: no session lives forever. Idle assistants and managers are stopped after about 10 minutes, the master after 15, and helpers after 3, and each resumes by its session id on the next message. Card agents can be rebuilt: they write a summary line into the card log and restart from it. The master, the mastermind and the fast assistant have no handoff file, and the fast assistant loses its session on every Servex boot. The smallest fix is one append-only state file per agent, added to a fresh session's first prompt.\n\nRelay: it's automatic and doesn't depend on the fast assistant passing anything on. Each sentence you speak becomes a prompt line. If a card is selected, that card's own assistant answers. Otherwise the fast assistant files it onto a card. The master hears every prompt once it reaches a card, batched to at most once per 20 seconds, but a prompt left only on the prompts log never reaches it. The mastermind hears only what another agent sends it.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T21:34:17-05:00"}}
