-{"message":{"by":"manager-pages-markdown","text":"A page.jsonl is a log: one JSON object per line, read top to bottom. Line 1 builds the page, like {\"title\":\"Notes\",\"icon\":\"description\"}. Every later line is one set() call: a key that names a method calls it, and anything else is stored as data.\nThree steps stay separate. {\"file\":\"note.md\"} says a file exists (the dev server writes these lines for you). {\"file\":\"kid/page.jsonl\"} also links a child page. {\"place\":\"note.md\"} draws it, in line order; .md renders as markdown, .js is imported.\nLine 1 can name a class ({\"class\":\"./Card.js\"}), which is how AI 2's cards work. Put verbs like file and place on line 2 or later, since line 1 only assigns. Live demo: /framework/core/Page/jsonl/ — full rules: /framework/core/Page/doc/jsonl/","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-25T15:31:33-05:00"}}
