-{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Dictate is on: a Sonnet minion is doing the box first. It gets a max height and scrolls inside itself. It then finds and fixes why the box jumps, and explains why the old italic line was steadier. It also measures the delay from Whisper's result to the box, in milliseconds, and fixes the odd paragraph breaks. Send-timing options, dictated text turned into structure beside the raw transcript, and the prompt-interpretation proposal follow. Names stay as they are.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T21:55:03-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"The dictation box is done and live, uncommitted, first part only. It grows to about 12 lines, then scrolls inside itself with the newest words in view. It jumped because at each pause Dictate blanked its guess and waited 100 to 300 ms for Whisper's final text, so the box collapsed and re-grew. Now the guess stays on screen until the final arrives, and the box never shrinks while you talk. Whitespace in the transcript is collapsed, and guesses are skipped once you are quiet. I do not have the delay numbers or the paragraph-break rule reported yet. The changes are in ux/Dictate/Dictate.js, ext/Chat/Mic.js and one line of ext/Chat/Chat.css.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T22:02:47-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Next minion started, on Dictate only, in ux/Dictate and ext/Chat/Mic.js. It fixes the paragraph breaks so they land only on real pauses, and measures the delay from Whisper's result to the box in milliseconds. It also makes Send never cut the live transcription. It builds three send modes with a demo you can click: manual (default), auto after a pause, and auto after three sentences. The box's height cap moves into Mic.js so it survives manager-new-card removing the Chat.css line.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T22:03:12-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Landed, live and uncommitted, tested headless with zero failed requests. Paragraph breaks now need a 1.5 s pause and a finished sentence. The delay is almost all Whisper: 67 ms for Whisper, and everything else under half a millisecond (box set 0.42). The other cost was a 1500 ms wait between guesses, now 900 ms. Send now sends only finished sentences while the mic is live, and the half-said one stays in the box. Default mode is manual, because nothing can send early. The other two, auto-send after a pause and after three sentences, are a switch. Click through all three at /framework/ux/Dictate/demo/. I have not confirmed where the demo is linked from.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T22:07:33-05:00"}}
