-{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-hidden-windows","text":"Found it. It's not a Node spawn bug — every detached+windowsHide spawn tested, even from a genuinely console-less parent, showed 0 visible windows. The real source: the \"Servex\" logon scheduled task runs `powershell.exe -WindowStyle Hidden`, and PowerShell hides its own window a moment AFTER Windows already shows it — a proven flash (reproduced by triggering the real task and watching for it). Fix: wrap the launch in a small .vbs (wscript.exe never has a console at all) — proven 0 visible windows. Two minions now: one applying that fix + a proper per-call enforcement check, one sweeping ~17 files with missing windowsHide the new repo-wide window-lint.mjs found. One thing I can't do myself: re-registering the live scheduled task needs your login password (schtasks asked for it and I backed off) — I'll leave the exact one-paste command in Servex/readme.md for you.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-28T11:10:49-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-ai2-lead-2","kind":"reply","text":"Fixed. Cause: another agent saved a page module at 11:00:21, which reloaded your AI 2 tab, and after a reload a group had no time until its members were read, so this row sorted near the bottom for a few seconds, then jumped back. The log was never rewritten. Now a group's time comes from the card index, which arrives with the first rows. Proof on the live site: the row is in view from the first paint on 3 reloads (before: 5 seconds off screen), and zero errors on the inbox, a card, this card and Now. Picture: /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-row-vanish/rail-1920.png","at":"2026-09-28T11:17:51-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-hidden-windows","text":"Landed. The popup's real cause: the Windows logon task that starts Servex runs `powershell -WindowStyle Hidden`, and PowerShell hides its own window a moment after Windows already shows it — proven by triggering the task and watching a real console appear. Fixed with a small .vbs wrapper (wscript.exe never has a console at all) — proven 0 visible windows. Also swept 17 files missing windowsHide and made the enforcement check (syntax-guard's hidden_guard) check every call instead of a rough per-file count, so a real gap can't hide behind an unrelated call in the same file. One thing left for you: re-pointing the actual running scheduled task needs your login password — the exact one-paste command is in Servex/readme.md, \"Surviving a reboot.\" Full report: public/framework/ai/2026-09-28/hidden-windows/","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-28T11:20:08-05:00"}}
-{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-hidden-windows","text":"Landed. One real cause found and fixed (the Servex logon task flashing a console — see earlier note). A second lead (a Playwright/Chromium popup) didn't reproduce after three faithful tries, so instead of more guessing there's now a live, hidden, always-on catcher (Server/window-watch.mjs) that logs any new console/browser window with its full process chain the next time it happens. Enforcement is in and hand-tested: every spawn/exec call gets checked individually now, not just a rough per-file count. Full report: public/framework/ai/2026-09-28/hidden-windows/","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-28T11:36:05-05:00"}}
