lls or sidebars or you know we have lots of different layouts and uh, It, it, it seems a little broken. I think we might have a few extra containers or something. Um, some of it might be optimal, but maybe we just need to tweak, you know, uh, some CSS or something. I'm not actually sure what's going on there. Um, but when it comes to having potentially multiple sidebars at multiple levels, um, you know, with, with the EXT drawers, I don't know if we have like named sidebars like app.com. Right or app dot left or or what you know we would want to name them but like having reusable uh, I mean I was asking I think yesterday about whether sidebars should be reusable or whether we sh you know and then they would have like a paging system within them to swap out you know when we render something into a column one of those sidebars and then we want to swap it out to some you know when we click on something else to select something else I'm not really sure how that works But also then like, well, what if we wanted to have multiple left sidebars or right sidebars? I'm not sure if we really want to, but we might want to. And how those are stored, I, I would imagine that we would want a handle, a good reference to each one in the app structure or in the page structure. So the page, any, well, the app could have a left and right sidebar drawer. It, well, either a persistent left or right sidebar, like a navigation. That may or may not collapse and then could also have a drawer that you know opens kind of above that as like a shell and a page could have a, a left sidebar drawer that opens you know within that and pushes things over I don't know there's a lot of different ways to to set that up but we definitely want to work on uh work on that system especially in this three column layout explorer because I'm not sure if we want the dev so we have the dev bar we have the right sidebar for you know like selecting It seems like it's uh, available now on, I don't know if it's on every page, but for selecting items within a page and, and, and talking about them. By the way, that seemed to be broken. Uh, I, I was able to select on, when I opened up the hamburger menu on the AI2 dashboard page, I was able to select an element and, um, and then I, I tried to do a dictation you know, to ask about that element I had selected and it said it didn't see the selected element. So it, it did appear in the UI. I selected a code block and it, it had a little label that said this code block and it had a little X on it, a little pill that was kind of that contextual UI that uh, a lot of AI systems have. Um, and so that seemed to work, but then when I sent the message off, the assistant, at least the fast assistant said, I don't see that. Context, so somehow the context isn't getting to, you know, pump, pumped through to the LLM as part of the prompt. 
