-{"content":{"add":{"id":"how","title":"How this card was made","text":"**The files.** A card is a folder named by its date; its whole content is one append-only log:\n\n```\npublic/framework/ai/2026/10/03/\n  page.jsonl        the day: lists its cards\n  now/\n    page.jsonl      this card: one JSON line per change\n```\n\n**The calls.** Three tool calls made it, each appending one line:\n\n```js\ncreate_card({ title: \"Now\", type: \"note\", summary: \"What the AI agents are doing…\" })\n// → line 1: {\"class\": \"/framework/ai2/card.js\", \"title\": \"Now\", \"type\": \"note\", …}\n\npage_add({ path: \"/framework/ai/2026/10/03/now/\",\n           item: { id: \"working\", title: \"Working on now\", text: \"- **Console cleanup:** …\" } })\n// → {\"content\": {\"add\": {\"id\": \"working\", \"title\": \"…\", \"text\": \"…\"}}}\n```\n\n**Loading it.** The page replays the log line by line: line 1 picks the class, each `content.add` adds an item to the page's `content` List. The list draws one row per item: its title, then its text as markdown.\n\n**Why the rows drag.** Every content list is drawn sortable on purpose (core/Page `render_content_list`): drop a row elsewhere and one `move` line is appended, so the order is saved like any other change. It's not specific to cards; any page with a content list gets it.","by":"agent","ts":"2026-10-03T17:57:20.634Z"}}}
