-{"working":{"title":"AI system: the dashboard you're reading","text":"**Landed today**\n- **Cards show their content:** a section's text appears under its title, on white cards over a gray background, and the card scrolls.\n- **No more 404 on Your prompts** (/framework/ai/your-prompts/).\n- **AI 2 is out of the menu**, the first step of retiring it.\n- **A data-corrupting edit bug fixed:** changing one section no longer blanks the card's title (Servex needs a restart to pick it up).\n- **A quiet console:** the ~100 missing-file errors on /framework/ai/live/ are gone, and a page with a noisy console can't be merged any more.\n\n**Working on now**\n- **Readable cards** (@task-mastermind-inbox-cards-work): previews that say something real, plain-word titles, the Activity tab bug.\n- **The drawer** (@task-mastermind-drawer-cleanup): a tight header, one scrolling chat area, the talk box pinned to the bottom with no double padding.\n- **The rest of AI 2** (@mastermind-ai-3): moving the code the new page still uses, then deleting the old folder."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:16:45-05:00"}
-{"fixed":{"title":"Page system: how every page stores and draws itself","text":"**Landed today**\n- **One simpler data model:** #Page extends #Item directly; a #List is an Item too; every value lives in `data`; a field that collides with a method now throws instead of failing silently.\n- **Simpler log lines:** no special `at` key; the nesting of a line IS its path (`{\"k2\": {\"title\": \"New\"}}`).\n- **Dragging is opt-in:** only a list marked `sortable` can be reordered, and a dragged row keeps its font.\n- **The AI cost line** moved to the bottom of each page.\n\n**Working on now**\n- **Framework home grids** (@task-mastermind-framework-home-grids): no gaps under short cards on /framework/, a switch that labels every grid.\n- **Layout check** (@task-mastermind-layout-gate): links styled the same everywhere; a merge fails when text touches its box's edge.\n- **Card widths and colours lab** (@task-mastermind-card-measure-colors): cards and flowing text on one margin; backgrounds that lighten or darken by what they sit on."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:16:45-05:00"}
-{"problems":{"title":"Servex and your machine","text":"**Landed today**\n- **Leftover dev servers cleaned up:** 13 node processes, down from 59; agents can no longer start their own servers.\n- **Every test browser is logged and closed** when its job ends; one shared browser lets me check a page's console for you (`check_page`).\n- **Spending follows results:** an agent gets more budget only after it shows something working.\n\n**Problems I know about**\n- **Masterminds fall asleep** when their first task lands, even with work queued. My hourly check-in wakes them until Servex does it itself.\n- **Usage is over pace:** 62% of the week used with 63% of it left, so agents run on Sonnet with small budgets."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:16:45-05:00"}
-{"content":{"add":{"id":"talking","title":"What you're talking about (newest first)","text":"- **A Chrome window popped up on your screen (1:19 pm).** An agent used the Playwright browser tool, which opened a visible window. I closed it and switched that tool to headless; agents should check pages through `check_page` instead.\n- **This card as our workspace.** Newest topics at the top; each system shown as its own dark page card (icon + name), with links to the right docs instead of descriptions.\n- **Referencing a page cheaply.** A page card needs only the page's icon and title, not the whole page. Today #Mention keeps a generated list of them (ext/Mention/maps/refs.js), but someone has to re-run its script, so it can go stale.\n- **The drawer:** tight header, one scrolling chat, talk box at the bottom.\n- **Cards and prose on one margin; padding by default; adaptive backgrounds.** Two lab pages coming.","by":"agent","ts":"2026-10-03T18:21:05.365Z","after":"null"}}}
