-{"talking":{"text":"- **Answers go here, not in the sidebar.** From now on I write my replies on this card; the sidebar gets a line and a link.\n- **Your prompts, refined live.** Each prompt you send appears on [its own sub-card](/framework/ai/2026/10/03/now/your-prompts-refined-live/) through a hook; a refiner turns it into numbered statements in front of you, nothing dropped; I reply under the statement I'm answering. Building: @task-mastermind-prompts-live (queued, 5 agents running).\n- **Sub-cards open in a column beside their card** (Miller columns): today opening the sub-card replaces this card with a back link. Building: @task-mastermind-subcard-columns (queued).\n- **How this card is stored.** One file, one line per change; each section is an item with an id (`talking`, `ai`, `page`, `servex`, `how`); edits name the id, never the position. Details in the \"How this card was made\" section.\n- **Dark context cards** for AI / Page / Servex: the text is now inside the reference rows; the dark look is with @mastermind-page-3.\n- **Is there a System class?** Not yet; started now: @task-mastermind-system-class.\n- **Chrome pop-ups:** blocked for every agent."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:36:35-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **Sub-cards: two equal columns that slide as you drill down.** The inbox rail stays as the monitor. The detail side becomes two equal columns: a card, then its sub-card beside it; one level deeper opens a third and hides the first, so you always see the last two levels, with a breadcrumb back. A link to a different page still links away. This matches your Sep 17 call (\"N even columns, not continuous Miller columns\") and reuses the /imagine/paging column work. Added to @task-mastermind-subcard-columns's brief before it starts.\n- **Answers go here, not in the sidebar.**\n- **Your prompts, refined live** on [their own sub-card](/framework/ai/2026/10/03/now/your-prompts-refined-live/): @task-mastermind-prompts-live (queued).\n- **How this card is stored:** one file, one line per change, each section an item with an id. See \"How this card was made\".\n- **Dark context cards** for AI / Page / Servex: with @mastermind-page-3.\n- **The System class:** being built, @task-mastermind-system-class.\n- **Chrome pop-ups:** blocked for every agent."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:39:32-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **Hourly check-in, 1:45 pm.** Landed since 1:17: the dark reference rows (AI / Page / Servex), links styled everywhere plus a merge check for text touching its edge, card text spacing and live @agent links, plain-word card titles, a navigation fix (one broken page no longer breaks every link after it), drags saved in the right place.\n- **Problem: Servex restarts are killing agents.** Two restarts in the last hour, both by agents. Three agents stopped mid-task without landing; the AI mastermind is gone. I revived the cards agent, restarted the sub-card columns agent (now @task-mastermind-subcard-columns-2, queued), and gave @mastermind-servex-10 the fix: restarts resume agents in place, and agents can't restart Servex mid-work.\n- **Usage is well over pace:** 64% of the week used, 38% of the week gone. At this rate we'd hit the weekly limit in about a day and a half, so I'm starting fewer agents: the framework home grids and the drawer wait until the cards and columns land.\n- **Sub-cards: two equal columns that slide as you drill down;** the inbox rail stays. Queued.\n- **Your prompts, refined live:** @task-mastermind-prompts-live is working.\n- **The System class:** @task-mastermind-system-class is working (converting the AI page now).\n- **Chrome pop-ups:** blocked for every agent."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:40:30-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **The sub-card page is cluttered; one talk box for everything.** Is \"Your prompts, refined live\" working? Not yet: the card exists and @task-mastermind-prompts-live is building it, so I marked it a request, status building. The template gets cleaned up by the sub-card columns agent: no per-card talk column (the one global drawer agent instead, since a fresh context per card knows less, not more); the right column becomes quiet card properties (type, status, who worked on it, files, Actions); \"nothing running · cost not tracked\" only shows when something runs; the back link gets padding.\n- **The font flashes on reload.** The app waits for fonts and stylesheets before first paint, so something drawn after that paints before its own CSS arrives (a card's stylesheet, the replayed log, or the live CSS swap). @mastermind-page-3 finds which and makes it wait.\n- **Hourly check-in, 1:40 pm.** Servex restarts by agents stopped three agents; revived and fixed at the source (@mastermind-servex-10). Usage well over pace (64% used, 38% of the week gone), so fewer agents at once.\n- **Sub-cards: two equal columns that slide as you drill down;** inbox rail stays. Queued: @task-mastermind-subcard-columns-2.\n- **The System class:** @task-mastermind-system-class is working.\n- **Chrome pop-ups:** blocked for every agent."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:43:37-05:00"}
