-{"talking":{"text":"- **A listener bound to this session, fed by the hook: that's exactly what was built, and it's broken somewhere.** Servex keeps one Echo agent per owner session; the prompt hook already knows this session's id and posts each prompt to it the moment you send it; Echo knows where the session's page is and writes the refinement there. Since yesterday's batch nothing has been refined, so one link in that chain is broken. @task-mastermind-prompts-live is finding which link and fixing only that.\n- **Why a new agent for prompt refinement? Mostly built already; I over-scoped it** and have cut it back to the fix above, $6.\n- **The sub-card page is cluttered; one talk box for everything.** With @task-mastermind-subcard-columns-2 (queued).\n- **The font flashes on reload.** With @mastermind-page-3.\n- **Usage well over pace** (64% used, 38% of the week gone): fewer agents at once."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:44:40-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **Refinement belongs in both dictation paths, and every prompt shows its cost.** The VS Code path (this tab, or your phone through remote control) goes hook → per-session listener: @task-mastermind-prompts-live is fixing that link. Your own Whisper dictation path makes refinement the FAST assistant's job: @task-mastermind-one-dictation checks it calls the same Refine engine and wires it if not. Every prompt gets its total cost (its length in tokens, the refinement's model cost, any Whisper/API cost), and the session page a running total, computed from real usage.\n- **New rule: a system isn't done until it's plugged in where it belongs.** Added to the finish-task skill: before landing, list the existing places that do the same job, wire in the cheap ones, and post a question card for a big or costly one instead of waiting. Fresh agent vs reusing one: fresh is fine when the readmes are good; reuse only a recent, small session.\n- **A listener bound to this session, fed by the hook, already exists;** one link in it is broken. Being fixed.\n- **The sub-card page is cluttered; one talk box for everything.** With @task-mastermind-subcard-columns-2 (queued).\n- **Usage well over pace** (64% used, 38% of the week gone): fewer agents at once."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:49:26-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **Next: each topic here becomes its own card you can click into** (queued until the prompt refiner and the sub-card columns land). Per prompt you'll see raw → cleaned → structured; each topic gets a sub-card with your statements, my answer and the agents on it; this list shrinks to titles. Changed items get a small \"updated\" mark, no flashing. [Brief](/framework/ai/2026-10-03/topic-cards/)\n- **The Now card is missing from the inbox list:** an old filter hides anything with the id \"now\". Being fixed by @task-mastermind-inbox-cards-work.\n- **Plugging new systems in: softened.** Only where it plainly makes sense, each as its own commit so it reverts cleanly; the costlier it is, the more it becomes a question for you instead.\n- **Git, Context and Cost as AI systems:** three pages that collect what we've already learned (Git habits; when to compact, start fresh or reuse an agent; how to decide by cost). Queued after the System class. [Brief](/framework/ai/2026-10-03/ai-git-context-cost/)\n- **Prompt refinement in both dictation paths, with a cost on every prompt.** Being fixed and wired.\n- **While you're away:** the hourly check-in keeps the queue moving at a slower pace, since usage is over (64% used, 38% of the week gone)."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T13:55:18-05:00"}
-{"talking":{"text":"- **Check-in, 2:39 pm: a lot landed.**\n  - **Sub-cards open beside their card:** two equal columns that slide as you drill down, a padded breadcrumb, and a quiet properties column instead of the per-card talk box.\n  - **Prompt refinement is running again:** the broken link was the refiner reading the old line format; fixed, with a cost on each prompt.\n  - **The drawer's scroll and footer** are fixed (a hidden dropdown that never closed was the cause).\n  - **No more font flash on AI pages:** pages now wait for their own code before the styles check.\n  - **Two labs:** card widths, and adaptive backgrounds with contrast ratios (in Styles).\n  - **Mention icons rebuild themselves** when a page's icon changes.\n- **Started: your topics as cards you can click into** (@task-mastermind-topic-cards).\n- **Problem: the System class got cut off again** by a Servex restart before it committed anything; revived (@task-mastermind-system-class). The restart fix with @mastermind-servex-10 hasn't landed yet.\n- **Holding back:** the framework home grids (cut off twice) and the Git/Context/Cost pages wait. Usage: 67% of the week used, 38% gone; at this rate we'd hit the limit in about two days, so two agents at a time."},"by":"vscode-mastermind","ts":"2026-10-03T14:39:43-05:00"}
