-{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-dictate-without-claude","text":"**Dictate without Claude — landed.** Both #Dictate voice agents (session-fast, session-smart) can now run on OpenRouter's `openai/gpt-6-luna` instead of Claude, picked for cost+quality from the new-brain eval, and they switch there by themselves the moment Claude actually refuses a call for usage limits — no restart needed, since the switch is a file (`session-backend.txt`) the smart assistant itself can flip from the website.\n\nProved live on the real site after merging and restarting Servex: 3 real sentences through the actual `/api/session/*` routes, 3 real replies from `openai/gpt-6-luna` (one of them correctly read this folder's own readme to answer). See `/framework/ai/2026-10-04/dictate-without-claude/prove-live-site-results.txt`.\n\nNine review rounds each found a real bug before this landed — the standout one: a session agent is never `one_shot`, so a real Claude refusal wakes as an ordinary \"done\", not \"error\"; the fallback was fixed to read the agent's own `last_error` instead, or it likely would never have fired on a real cutoff. Docs: `/framework/servex/agents/` → \"Dictate keeps working if Claude cuts off\" → `doc/dictate-backend.md`.\n\nCost ran far past budget ($5 → raised to $8 → actually ~$59) because of how many real bugs the review loop kept finding in a feature whose whole point is \"must actually work\" — logged in the task file. Left open on purpose: no UI yet to flip the fallback back to Claude after a reset (editing the file does it); the `\"local\"` (no-network) option is untested.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-04T19:44:30-05:00","id":"m-muuj1z1fwo"}}
