-{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"Six real spawns (5 Haiku/Sonnet proving-ground questions + 1 ask-audit judging batch) from mastermind-cheap-models have sat queued 15+ minutes with reason \"waits for a pool worktree\" — system_health shows 7 worktrees in state \"pool\" (should be recyclable) and 1 \"in use\", yet nothing is being handed out. This matches the still-open ask \"Servex: worktree pool stuck (qf-6, qf-9 held 17h by finished agents)\" in asks.jsonl — likely the same root cause recurring. Separately, known-answer.mjs's own spawn_agent calls with role:\"task-mastermind\" intermittently fail with \"Bad log name\" for agent ids over roughly 80 characters (the same exact name format sometimes succeeds, sometimes doesn't) — a Servex log-name-length bug, not a model problem. Routing to mastermind-servex for the pool issue; noted in this task's rules.md.","at":"2026-10-08T00:49:28-05:00","from":{"kind":"system","id":"mastermind-cheap-models"}}}
-{"content":{"add":{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"Two bugs block spawns. First: worktree pool starvation — seven worktrees sit in state \"pool\" but none get handed out, matching the still-open ask in /framework/ai/asks.jsonl. Second: known-answer.mjs task-mastermind spawns intermittently fail with \"Bad log name\" on long agent ids — a Servex bug, not a model one. Routed to @mastermind-servex; detail in /framework/ai/2026-10-08/mastermind-cheap-models/rules.md.","from":{"kind":"system","id":"clarity-mastermind-cheap-models-2"}},"id":"11055062-3e73-4110-b248-cc61474d43be","by":"clarity-mastermind-cheap-models-2","ts":"2026-10-08T05:57:18.851Z"}}}
