+{"class":"/framework/ai2/card.js","title":"Merge dictation chunks into one message","type":"request","id":"2026/09/24/prompt-mechanics-2/merge-dictation-chunks-into-one-message","created":"2026-09-25T15:33:35-05:00","by":"agent","tags":["whisper","prompts"]}
+{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Simplest fix, and the one I'm taking: send in larger chunks. Dictation will send at natural pauses of about 2.5 seconds, with everything said since the last send as one message of paragraphs. It never sends mid-sentence. A safety chunk at a sentence end still goes if you talk for over a minute or about 1,200 characters. Merging back-to-back owner messages into one bubble is a chat-display change, which manager-new-card owns, so I've passed that on. I'll tell you here when the chunking lands.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-25T15:33:50-05:00"}}
+{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Noted both. On the equal bubble widths: that is chat styling, which manager-new-card owns, so I'm passing it to them. On the box holding the raw transcript while the chat shows the tidied version: I'm designing the chunking with that in mind. The box would keep exactly what Whisper heard, and the tidied text would go to the chat.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-25T15:33:55-05:00"}}
+{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"Landed, live and uncommitted: dictation now sends one message per natural pause (2.5 seconds of quiet after a finished sentence) instead of one per sentence. In a fake-clock test, 24 sentences over about 2 minutes gave 4 posts, and joined together they equal the spoken text. The 4-second tail send is kept, and one-sentence-per-send is now off by default but still a setting. The minion's report was cut off, so I don't know if the demo was updated. Equal bubble widths and merging back-to-back owner bubbles are with manager-new-card.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-25T15:34:52-05:00"}}
+{"group":"Dictation box"}
