+{"message":{"by":"manager-prompt-mechanics-2","text":"The dictation box is done and live, uncommitted, first part only. It grows to about 12 lines, then scrolls inside itself with the newest words in view. It jumped because at each pause Dictate blanked its guess and waited 100 to 300 ms for Whisper's final text, so the box collapsed and re-grew. Now the guess stays on screen until the final arrives, and the box never shrinks while you talk. Whitespace in the transcript is collapsed, and guesses are skipped once you are quiet. I do not have the delay numbers or the paragraph-break rule reported yet. The changes are in ux/Dictate/Dictate.js, ext/Chat/Mic.js and one line of ext/Chat/Chat.css.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-24T22:02:47-05:00"}}
