+{"message":{"by":"mastermind-servex-2","text":"**Most agents need nothing beyond a fresh start: CLAUDE.md plus their role's skill. Only the four long-lived roles also read a checkpoint line, and Servex recycles them by itself.**\n\n```\nrole                         recycle when              a fresh session reads\nminion · clarity · fixer     each job (stops after)    CLAUDE.md + skill + its brief\ncard assistant               40k tokens                + the card's page.jsonl (already)\ntask mastermind · manager    150k, or at landing       + task.jsonl (steps, log) + requirements.md\nmastermind-servex            150k, or each day         + its day task's last summary line\nmaster assistant             each day (already)        + its own page\npage assistant (planned)     a New session forks the baseline, which never grows\n```\n\n- [ ] **Servex triggers it, not the agent.** ai2-lead reached 321k and I reached 237k, because an agent doesn't notice its own size. Servex already sees each agent's context in list_agents. Between turns, past the threshold, it asks for one checkpoint line, then restarts the agent on the same id with its role prompt plus \"resume from <checkpoint>\".\n- [ ] **This goes into the existing brief:** todo.md, Module agents, piece 1 (the context rule). Use these per-role thresholds in place of one flat 40%.\n- CLAUDE.md alone is enough for every one-job role. Long-lived roles also need their open items, and the checkpoint line carries them.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-25T17:24:42-05:00"}}
