e like an initial phase where everyone goes and does their, you know, you give them the initial prompt and then they, when they're done, when everyone's done and they've all written it down into their directory or whatever. And so on one work tree, you could have each, each minion create their own directory in that, you know, work work folder or where, whatever directory you're working in, then each uh, minion can read. I don't know if you have all the minions read each other's, but, you know, or maybe it's just the mastermind reads. I don't know if the mastermind should read them all or if the, they should all work together. If the mastermind reads all of them and tries to make conclusions, that's going to, you know, fry the, the mastermind's like context uh, or focus, I think. So maybe you have each of the minions read maybe one or two others and then revise their own and um i don't know that that whole process of, of reaching the consensus maybe the research system has some way to like you know for each of the minions to give feedback about each kind of idea so okay here this is what makes sense if we had let's say a dozen minions building the same thing you need to we need to figure out a way to refine the potential into the actual outcome so like the name of the class the name of the properties and the names of the methods those are all very tangible things so for object oriented design you know we should be able to systematically create a consensus mechanism to vote on the best name and the best method names and property names and method arguments and, and whatever, like the, the core structure. And then from there, the, uh, the minions could design, well, first, once you reach consensus, then you move forward and you have them each design, those, or like write the code for those methods and get it working. And then through that process, you know, they're gonna learn a lot in terms of like what needs to happen and, and which problems to solve. And, and then they could kind of review each other's code again and say, okay, you know, which one, Are these like functionally identical and are there any improvements we could make to any of them to make them the, you know, whichever, I don't know how you arrive at the best method, you know, um, maybe the, each minion just votes on which one they, they pick the best one. And then the one that gets the, the most votes becomes the right one. And maybe, maybe the, the minions can choose their favorite essentially with, uh, any improvements they would recommend or caveats that, you know, might be. Uh, important. And so that way, you know, you could get simultaneously the, the choice, you know, try and arrive at a decision and, uh, and also like be aware if, if, you know, maybe one, the best option is this one, but it's missing, you know, some important caveat. And so if you just add another extra line or fix one little thing, then it's, you know, clearly the best.
