+{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-ai2-lead-2","kind":"reply","text":"Live: the Page class is a row in your inbox, and clicking it opens the real /framework/core/Page/ page in the detail area, full height, tabs working. Try it: /framework/ai2/framework/core/Page/ . Servex works the same way. Your two questions: 1) Yes, any site page can show there as the same page, with no change to core; AI 2 asks the site router for it and moves its view in. 2) A row knows its page from its events: any log line that says \"page\": \"/framework/core/Page/\" bumps that page to the top. Picture: /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-real-pages/shot-page-row-3440.png . Details: /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-real-pages/answers.md . Tasks living in class folders: a proposal only, nothing moved: /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-real-pages/proposal-tasks.md (for mastermind-servex-3). The drawer is told which page is open, but I cannot show it until the page drawer merges. Next: the Overview sized by importance.","at":"2026-09-28T14:46:54-05:00"}}
+{"message":{"by":"mastermind-servex-3","text":"Decided: a task about one page lives in that page's folder, at `<page>/ai/<date>-<slug>/`. I accepted ai2-lead-2's proposal with one change: the folder is `ai/`, not `tasks/`, because the drawer's sessions already live there and one folder per page keeps modules clean. That `ai/` folder stays out of the Docs tree and the file browser, and shows in the drawer's Sessions tab. A task that spans pages stays in `ai/<date>/`. Nothing old moves until you've seen it.\n\nReady to dispatch #16 after task-loop lands: role `task-mastermind`, name `task-placement`, `claude-sonnet-5`, medium, `bypassPermissions`, brief ai/2026-09-28/task-placement/requirements.md.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-09-28T14:47:28-05:00"}}
+{"message":{"by":"task-mastermind-ai2-lead-2","kind":"reply","text":"You asked what the small WORKSPACE word is. It is an experiment: on a card with tabs (like System design), it turns the card into a centred page with its own left nav. On other rows it does nothing, which is why it looked dead. Before (normal): /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-workspace/shots/ai2w-system-design-3440-off.png . After (workspace on): /framework/ai/2026-09-28/ai2-workspace/shots/ai2w-system-design-3440-on.png . Fix under way: the word will show only where it works, labelled \"Floating page view (try it)\". Your real-page direction mostly supersedes it; say the word and I remove it.","at":"2026-09-28T22:45:53-05:00"}}
