+{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"Push-to-talk gets a second mode: Ctrl+Shift+M toggles an open mic; the floating mic shows only while the microphone is live. Queued after it: when you describe something on the page, each utterance carries a compact list of what's visible (headings and items, each with an address, a few hundred tokens, never the raw log); the fast assistant names the element, the smart one answers the same question without seeing that answer, and if they agree the element is highlighted. The blind check becomes a general rule for the pair. Brief: /framework/ai/2026-10-03/point-at-it/","at":"2026-10-03T16:46:34-05:00","from":{"kind":"system","id":"vscode-mastermind"}}}
+{"content":{"add":{"id":"select","title":"Or just point: Ctrl+Shift+click","text":"- **Hold Ctrl+Shift and click anything** to select it for the AI. Plain clicks stay normal; Escape clears.\n- **It selects the meaningful thing first:** clicking the icon inside an icon item selects the whole item; a drill-down mode reaches its children.\n- **A small popover** shows what you picked (its icon and name, or just \"div\") and its tree: parents above, children below, each clickable.\n- **The address is exact:** an item's id when it has one, otherwise its position plus the moment it was taken (\"as of 4:52 pm\"), so nothing has to guess. Your next words carry the selection, so \"fix this\" needs no matching at all.\n- **Built on what exists:** the drawer's inspect-mode selection and the old \"pick an element\" tool.","by":"agent","ts":"2026-10-03T21:50:28.704Z"}}}
