+{"class":"/framework/ai2/card.js","title":"Core/Page: Mastermind pilot","type":"task","id":"2026/10/05/core-page-mastermind-pilot","created":"2026-10-05T15:29:47-05:00","by":"v-yxnts4l","tags":["core-page","servex"]}
+{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"Run a small pilot of a task-specific Core/Page mastermind using Servex's worktree workflow. Map the Page class and its owned subsystems from the readme chain, then report a concise first-step plan and how the mastermind will keep work moving. Use OpenRouter only to preserve Anthropic quota; do not edit code during this pilot. Track this request on the card.","at":"2026-10-05T15:29:47-05:00","from":{"kind":"system","id":"v-yxnts4l"}}}
+{"file":"ai/"}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Scope clarification: the Page mastermind is a durable domain expert for `public/framework/core/Page/` and its subsystems: page creation/structure and live-tail behavior. Its working directory should be the Page module, with the root-to-module readme chain loaded automatically at startup. This is a real pilot of the mastermind workflow, not merely a page-system document proposal.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:08:43-05:00","id":"m-muvqsc0j4t"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Launch attempt outcome: Servex rejected this voice smart-assistant session's `spawn_agent` call with `may not spawn a task-mastermind: a worker may spawn only a minion or a helper.` No agent or worktree was created. This confirms the current permission boundary blocks the smart assistant from launching the requested mastermind; it must be handed to an authorized parent/manager or the architecture changed through the proper system owner.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:13:32-05:00","id":"m-muvqyiktrk"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner approved the handoff. I attempted to route the task to `mastermind-servex`, but this smart-assistant session is not authorized to message that coordinator directly. I left a note on `/framework/servex/` for the authorized coordinator to pick up. No launch/worktree has yet been verified.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:14:01-05:00","id":"m-muvqz52iyt"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Verified blocker: Servex `Policy.kind()` classifies `session-smart-v-yxnts4l` as a generic worker because it matches none of the known role prefixes (`Servex/agents/policy.js:42`). `Policy.spawn()` therefore applies the worker rule and refuses `task-mastermind` (`policy.js:124`). This is a deterministic role-policy mismatch, not an AI judgment. The smart assistant needs a narrow ability to launch task masterminds while staying unable to spawn/manage minions. I left this finding and requested an authorized Servex policy fix on `/framework/servex/`.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:16:31-05:00","id":"m-muvr2d11cv"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner explicitly says identity should not be spoofed by prompt. The right fix is in trusted caller classification/policy: recognize the smart voice-session role and allow it to spawn only `task-mastermind` (with tests); keep ordinary workers limited to minion/helper, keep the assistant unable to spawn minions/managers, and ensure the raw role/alias path cannot bypass that restriction. Please have the authorized Servex owner implement and test this in a clean worktree; do not edit the dirty shared tree.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:17:06-05:00","id":"m-muvr341nuw"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner explicitly authorized fixing the spawn policy. Exact safe behavior requested: trusted smart voice sessions may launch only `task-mastermind`; they must not gain minion/helper/manager spawning. Generic workers remain minion/helper-only. Add policy tests for both allowed and denied paths; caller role must come from Servex-trusted context, never prompt text. This session cannot edit Servex or spawn the needed task mastermind, so the `/framework/servex/` page note requests the authorized Servex mastermind to implement it in a clean worktree.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:17:26-05:00","id":"m-muvr3jmgpq"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner clarifies the desired fix is broader than this Page pilot: smart assistant needs a safe general ability to launch appropriate independent agents, particularly masterminds that own tasks and can manage their workers; it should not manage minions itself. Current state remains: root cause verified in policy.js; no policy code change, agent launch, or worktree yet. The requested Servex policy note is pending response.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:20:13-05:00","id":"m-muvr73zs7b"}}
