+{"class":"/framework/ai2/card.js","title":"Dictate: Find duplicate chat append","type":"task","id":"2026/10/05/voice-chat-cards-and-model-context/dictate-find-duplicate-chat-append","created":"2026-10-05T14:44:34-05:00","by":"v-yxnts4l","tags":["voice","dictate","bug"]}
+{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"Trace how a dictated owner message reaches and appends to chat bubbles, including the chat class outside Dictate if applicable. Identify why the same message is appended twice and report verified root cause with a minimal fix proposal. Investigate only; do not edit files until the cause/proposal is visible.","at":"2026-10-05T14:44:34-05:00","from":{"kind":"system","id":"v-yxnts4l"}}}
+{"note":{"id":"n-q67j03sm","from":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner authorizes the investigator to implement a reasonable in-scope fix once the duplicate-message cause is verified, rather than stopping at diagnosis. Preserve prior chat history; reproduce on current michael/dev; use OpenRouter only; prove the fix and report status. This supersedes the proposal-only constraint.","at":"2026-10-05T15:51:31.356-05:00"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Please reproduce and fix the duplicate cards in a worktree, then verify the fix. If live voice cannot be replayed because no audio fixture exists, trace the browser/microphone event path and test the underlying append handler with a controlled input; use Playwright if the available setup supports it. Preserve all prior chat entries. OpenRouter only.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T15:58:31-05:00","id":"m-muvqf7yjlt"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Also capture the operating-context requirement for new workers: load current project state and the repo's CLAUDE.md/system rules into their initial context, and read readmes from repo root through the active module. The owner expects a Dictate/domain mastermind to plan, delegate and track this work; avoid extra agents if one existing investigator can own it.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T15:59:16-05:00","id":"m-muvqg6qdei"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Additional concern to verify before relying on worktree previews: clarify whether a worktree's separate dev-server port/site also isolates runtime data or resolves some paths back to the shared Servex/repository locations. Prefer the pool's dedicated server; report the actual data-path behavior and use a controlled UI/append test if no audio fixture is available. Keep this part scoped; the immediate deliverable remains the duplicate-message fix and proof.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T15:59:52-05:00","id":"m-muvqgycr15"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Clarification: worktrees are wanted mainly as a safe sandbox for UI changes so they cannot break the main site. Do not expand this task into making all Servex/data locations operate independently in a worktree; just use the isolated worktree/dev server to test the Dictate UI fix.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T15:59:58-05:00","id":"m-muvqh2s7y1"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Please follow `public/framework/ai/v-yxnts4l.jsonl` for live corrections. Current operating direction is: fix and verify the Dictate duplicate in a worktree sandbox; don't turn it into a separate Servex/data-isolation project. Future task agents should have current system rules/state and the root-to-module readme chain available at startup.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:00:16-05:00","id":"m-muvqhgl84k"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner’s direction for the mastermind pilot: the mastermind should own the worktree lifecycle, delegate focused implementation to minions, verify the result, and merge only when it passes. Treat this Dictate fix as a chance to test that end-to-end workflow; report any workflow gaps rather than bypassing the gate.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:00:23-05:00","id":"m-muvqhm1asz"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner confirms duplicate items are still appearing. This remains unresolved and highest priority; do not mark it done or assume an investigator/worktree is active. Reproduce and fix in the existing task, then verify the UI behavior in a worktree before merge.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:09:50-05:00","id":"m-muvqtrxx7p"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"New observed symptom: the owner's “yeah, do that” arrived visibly above a smart-assistant reply they had already seen, making message order appear to jump. Investigate whether asynchronous incoming owner lines and assistant/tool replies can be rendered out of order, alongside duplicate appends; preserve existing chat history.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:13:56-05:00","id":"m-muvqz1l78s"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner says message timing and placement should be handled by the Dictate mastermind. Ensure investigation covers out-of-order display as well as duplicate appends; check event timestamps/order and the live chat rendering path, preserve history, and report the verified cause.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T16:14:16-05:00","id":"m-muvqzh428j"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"New incident at 17:01:20: owner saw red UI error “whisper has gone quiet” and transcription stopped. At 17:01:31 the supervised Whisper endpoint on 127.0.0.1:8178 returned HTTP 200; supervisor logs show it started at 16:25:38 and finished loading the CUDA model by 16:25:39, with no restart count/error shown. Investigate why Dictate's health check reported whisper-down while the endpoint is currently responding, including stale/shared detection timing. Do not restart a healthy service without evidence.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T17:02:10-05:00","id":"m-muvsp2qp5j"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Follow-up: after the 17:01 “whisper has gone quiet” report, Whisper's local `/` endpoint returned HTTP 200 during health checks, and subsequent owner dictations were received by Servex, indicating transcription recovered. No service restart was performed. The incident appears transient; investigate the 2.5s client health-check timeout/shared detection path and remote/mobile proxy route, but avoid changing behavior without reproduction.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T17:02:53-05:00","id":"m-muvsq00nki"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Second report at 17:23:39: owner still cannot transcribe. At 17:23:44 local Whisper `/` returned HTTP 200 in <1ms, and `http://monorepo.localhost/whisper/` proxy returned HTTP 200 too. This confirms health-page reachability from desktop, not mic capture or `/inference`. No restart performed. Investigate actual browser capture/inference failure and distinguish stale health/init error from POST transcription errors.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T17:24:11-05:00","id":"m-muvthdktl8"}}
+{"message":{"by":"session-smart-v-yxnts4l","text":"Owner reports at 17:28:48 the Dictate diagnostics say `Whisper not reachable`, `mic refused`, `socket retrying`. Desktop local Whisper and same-origin monorepo proxy both still return HTTP 200. This strongly points to a client-specific path (e.g. phone/LAN URL/proxy/Host guard) or exact URL/origin mismatch; test LAN proxy behavior before restarting the healthy local service.","kind":"reply","at":"2026-10-05T17:29:41-05:00","id":"m-muvtogrzcq"}}
