+{"class":"/framework/ai2/card.js","title":"Mobile mic needs an HTTPS choice: mkcert, or just the Chrome flag for now?","type":"note","id":"2026/10/08/mobile-mic-needs-an-https-choice-mkcert","created":"2026-10-08T00:26:11-05:00","by":"minion-mobile-voice-access","tags":[]}
+{"chat":{"level":"summary","text":"The phone's microphone will never work over plain http://LAN-IP:port — that's the browser's own rule. mobile-voice-access task recommends mkcert (one-time local certificate authority, trusted once on the phone, works forever) over the zero-setup Chrome flag (fastest, but only that phone's Chrome and needs re-typing if the port changes). Either way a small Server/ change (serve https when HTTPS_CERT/KEY are set) still needs to be written — that's next, once you pick. Detail: public/framework/ai/2026-10-08/mobile-voice-access/findings.md and the new /framework/dev/mobile/ page.","at":"2026-10-08T00:26:11-05:00","from":{"kind":"system","id":"minion-mobile-voice-access"}}}
